From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:52:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Small props' and the honey tree's sun shadows; a building's
 on higher ground re-laid (SDK_PORT_3DS)

A small prop's shadow (a bench, a rock, a sign) is now its outline, as a
building's: the hull of its model's vertices moved along the light (the
light's way turned into the model's own coordinates for a prop turned
about its upright), with a soft edge half as wide, and its own painted
shadow left out. Its mark gets 0x20000000: the port doesn't lay its
picture (with the sun to the side a bench's was a sliver).

The honey tree (honey_tree.nsbmd) is three layers over a painted patch,
as a land tree is: it's drawn through the land's trees' lists
(LandData_PortDrawTreeProp; its texture treeeff01 among the trees'),
its shadow the trees' outline. A tree shape with nothing but its stumps
sends no empty list.

A building's shadow on higher ground was the one on its own ground moved
up, as long and as far out: the Hallowed Tower's showed as two. Now the
shadow of what stands above that ground (NitroPort_Gx3dShadowHullPartsFrom),
for up to two heights found most often on a grid of tiles inside its
whole outline (first at its corners alone), the same for all its parts.
